      "type": "转发",
      "type_label": "转发",
      "text": "Balanced piece by Judge: the civil service is 12% smaller, cuts to grants far less steep than even I had hoped, but done well overall.\n\n\"By most indications, the federal government is running much as it did before. Some critics may have to admit: the DOGE workforce cuts worked.\"",
      "quote": {
        "author": "judgeglock",
        "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/818550134061428736/94IVwfrj_200x200.jpg",
        "created_at_shanghai": "2026-10-15 19:47:14",
        "created_at_utc": "2026-10-15T11:47:14.000Z",
        "id": "2110699013020565510",
        "images": [],
        "media": [],
        "name": "Judge Glock",
        "text": "DOGE worked. Most importantly, the civil service is 12% smaller than it was in Jan 2025.\n\nIn the Fall @CityJournal, I show they were not replaced by contractors, the biggest cuts were to middle managers, and the predictions of disaster were proven false. https://www.city-journal.org/article/doge-spending-cuts-civil-service-elon-musk",
        "url": "https://x.com/judgeglock/status/2110699013020565510",
        "verified": true,
        "verified_type": "individual"
      },
      "retweet": {
        "author": "JTLonsdale",
        "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1966994607880749056/78CHlGj__200x200.jpg",
        "created_at_shanghai": "2026-10-16 01:02:50",
        "created_at_utc": "2026-10-15T17:02:50.000Z",
        "id": "2110778437065691511",
        "images": [],
        "media": [],
        "name": "Joe Lonsdale",
